[{"code":"output_path_collision","severity":"error","span":{"file":"platform/Prog.js","start":{"line":1,"col":1},"end":{"line":1,"col":1}},"title":"OUTPUT PATHS COLLIDE","message":"Two files this build would write have the same name on a case-insensitive\nfile system:\n\n- `_platform/Prog.foreign.mjs`, written for `platform/Prog.js`\n- `_platform/PROG.foreign.mjs`, written for `platform/js/PROG.js`\n\nmacOS (APFS) and Windows (NTFS) fold case, so those are ONE file there and\nthe second would overwrite the first — the build would exit 0 and the program\nwould throw at load. A build's output is the same set of files on every file\nsystem (`docs/design/backend.md` §2), so this is refused and nothing is\nwritten. Rename one of the two sources."}]
